  "selection_rule": "Frozen paired severe-fault case must leave the unsupervised branch without CAD-bottom verification and expose its subsequent inactive-display raw-wrench violation; the supervised branch must reject CAD-depth overshoot without either a primary or post-event hard stop. This case is not a successful-recovery selector.",
  "claim_boundary": "Real MuJoCo paired mechanism stress demo with deliberately severe synthetic residual pose error: 8 deg orientation command and 0.6 mm lateral TCP disturbance exceed the nominal M8 deep-clearance scale. The current controller correctly treats the resulting CAD-depth overshoot as an unrecoverable terminal event and performs a named safe abort without a raw-wrench violation. The unsupervised branch first returns bottom-not-verified and then exceeds the raw limit on the explicitly labelled inactive display step; that late step is not relabelled as the primary terminal outcome. This trial does not exercise the full unload/retract/upright/retouch restart branch. It is not evidence of recovery success, fault frequency, hardware robustness, strict passivity, or a larger nominal task success rate."
